    {
      "id": "ledger-notes",
      "kind": {
        "text": "The deduction theorem proper says: Gamma together with p proves q if and only if Gamma proves (p implies q). That is a metatheorem -- it quantifies over derivations in a proof system, and this repository has no object for a derivation, so it cannot be stated. What CAN be stated is its semantic shadow at the object level, which is exportation, and that is what is recorded here. The gap between the two is exactly the gap between a solver and a proof assistant, and it is deliberate that this fact does not pretend to close it.\n\nOn the axiom footprint: it names the trust base of the SMT ROUTE that established this fact -- the axeyum-ir Boolean evaluator, and the two-valued semantics of the SMT-LIB Bool sort that makes exhaustive truth-table enumeration a proof. It is deliberately NOT empty and deliberately NOT a Lean axiom list. Nothing here went through axeyum's Lean kernel. Measured 2026-08-14 with `cargo run -q -p axeyum-lean-kernel --example nat_axiom_inventory`: the `logic` prelude reports axiom=0 opaque=0 quotient=0, and its declarations are exactly True, False, And, Or, Iff, Not (as `a -> False`), Eq and Exists -- an intuitionistic core with no `Classical.em`, no `propext` and no `Quot.sound`. Zero trusted declarations there means the kernel assumes nothing, not that it can prove everything.",
        "type": "prose"
      },
      "provenance": {
        "command": "python3 render/producers-py/facts_to_docir.py",
        "epoch": {
          "commit": "733126c0f351f0931f7eaf0b4f5f9f569f3aef44",
          "source": "commit",
          "unix": 1787338967
        },
